- op: discuss  # 7b99
  at: '2026-11-13T15:50:00Z'  # 7b99
  by: agent  # 7b99
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7b99
  clock: 4  # 7b99
  nonce: 7b99  # 7b99
  message: "Fixed in the PR that merged as dev's \"fix(compact): a budget tier slims every section and uses the budget it has\" (2026-11-13). WHAT SHIPPED: tier_projection.py gives every part of a tier a tier form: limits.skipped_passes / failed_files grouped into skipped_passes_by_reason / failed_files_by_reason (the ungrouped keys are absent from a tier); every list under a section the node selection does not own is cut to a budget-dependent cap (2 at 4k, 8 at 16k, 20 from 40k) with <key>_total beside it, a list of sentences (the caveat lists) kept whole, sections added later covered by the same walk; edges, entry points and features slimmed like nodes with the pointer invariant intact. The over-shrink recorded here from #2168 is gone: the selection is found by bisection over the fixed removal order, each probe measuring the written file. A run warns on stderr for a tier over budget with one node kept. EVIDENCE (hypergumbo survey, tier files read from disk, tokens used / nodes), before (after #2168) -> after: alertmanager 4k 6854/1 -> 3810/7, 16k 10323/13 -> 15377/43, 64k 56798/121 -> 63836/218; killbill 4k 13854/1 -> 3958/4, 16k 13814/1 -> 15906/38, 64k 58303/96 -> 63808/183; kserve 4k 8240/1 -> 3910/4, 16k 8227/1 -> 15405/35, 64k 58202/101 -> 63562/163; hypergumbo (before = the files the reviewer read) 4k 6698/1 -> 3820/2, 16k 16715/19 -> 15813/37, 64k 73678/143 -> 63354/168. All twelve files are within budget on disk and tier_tokens_used equals bytes // 4. A two-function repo's 4k and 16k tiers hold both functions and the run prints no warning (test_a_tier_that_cannot_meet_its_budget_warns_and_the_others_do_not). Eleven mutations each went red. COST: the bisection takes about 2 s on killbill's 64k tier (36,581 nodes, 156,429 edges); the 7 s that tier takes in all is the existing connectivity selection. NOT DONE: (1) profile.languages is a dict and is not cut; on hypergumbo the sections outside the node selection still take about 2.6k of the 4k tier (profile 860 tokens, limits 412, nodes_summary 383, reproducibility_context 371, supply_chain_summary 307, metrics 234). (2) Indentation is about a quarter of every tier file; the layout was left alone. (3) Node ids are still repeated across nodes, edges, entry points and features. (4) What the small tiers CHOOSE is unchanged: hypergumbo's 4k tier is two tracker HTTP handlers (WI-buvaf)."  # 7b99
